WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:05.270
I really enjoyed Disney's live-action Beauty
And The Beast and I loved the way it even

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:09.190
acknowledged and fixed some plot holes and
mistakes from the original animated movie,

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:12.620
but hidden in the new movie is another bunch
of new mistakes.

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:16.660
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here
and in this video, I'm going to break down

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:21.800
all the movie mistakes, goofs and plot holes
I spotted in Disney's 2017 Beauty And The

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:22.800
Beast.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:26.840
And if you'd like a chance to win this beautiful
hardback book "Tale as Old as Time: The Art

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:30.940
And Making of Beauty And The Beast", all you
need to do is subscribe, and leave a comment

00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:35.250
about the movie, and also answer the question
I'll be asking later in the video.

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:39.329
Quick warning there are some spoilers ahead
if you haven't seen the film.

00:00:39.329 --> 00:00:43.560
The movie's remake of the opening song "Belle"
is a lot of fun, but it still has its share

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:45.520
of continuity and logic errors!

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:49.831
For starters, there's something rather wrong
with the town clock bells as they ring 7 of

00:00:49.831 --> 00:00:52.940
the 8 bells before the clock has struck eight.

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:58.881
Belle then goes to pet one of the horses.

00:00:58.881 --> 00:01:02.210
Look carefully at the double loop of rope
around the horse's face which as Belle turns

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:05.870
to Monsieur Jean magically becomes a single
loop.

00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:10.350
Next, Belle goes over to Monsieur Jean and,
out of thin air, appears to conjure an apple,

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:11.810
which she gives to his donkey.

00:01:11.810 --> 00:01:15.869
However, if you look at Belle's skirt as she
leaves, there doesn't appear to be a pocket

00:01:15.869 --> 00:01:20.149
on the right-hand side of her dress where
the apple seemed to come from.

00:01:20.149 --> 00:01:24.959
And the knot tied around Monsieur Jean's donkey
also changes when going from this wide shot

00:01:24.959 --> 00:01:29.430
to a close-up shot of Belle feeding him the
apple.

00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:35.530
Now, keep your eye on the baguette Belle bought
from the baker which she put in her skirt

00:01:35.530 --> 00:01:40.509
pocket, because as we get to the next scene,
whoops the bread is gone!

00:01:40.509 --> 00:01:44.530
This particular mistake might be explained
by a scene which was deleted from the final

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:49.229
movie, in which Belle gives the beggar woman
Agathe, aka the Enchantress, a loaf of bread

00:01:49.229 --> 00:01:51.130
and a pot of jam.

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:55.599
Unfortunately, though, even taking into account
that deleted scene, this is still a mistake

00:01:55.599 --> 00:01:58.649
because the baguette still disappears too
early in the song.

00:01:58.649 --> 00:02:02.590
For example, here where Belle buys the jam,
which she later gives to Agathe with the bread

00:02:02.590 --> 00:02:05.520
in the deleted scene, the bread is already
missing.

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:10.110
I don't know, maybe Marie stole the baguette
in protest at not getting a mention in the

00:02:10.110 --> 00:02:12.500
new movie's opening song.

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:15.450
Belle's skirt is also a source of more continuity
errors.

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:20.000
Notice when she starts the song "Belle", her
skirt is hitched up on her right hand-side

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:22.160
revealing some of the white petticoat underneath.

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:26.640
The skirt stays hitched up through the song
until Belle enters the priest's library where

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:28.280
it's suddenly down.

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:33.160
As she entered the library, her hand did seem
to move towards her skirt, but that was the

00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:37.320
opposite side of where the skirt was hitched
up, and I suspect she was just reaching into

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:40.601
one of her skirt pockets for the book she
mentioned she was returning to Pere Robert.

00:02:40.601 --> 00:02:46.810
There's a funny moment when Gaston's horse
kicks mud all over the three lasses, ruining

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:48.040
their pink dresses.

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:52.251
However, when LeFou goes over to tell them,
"It's never going to happen ladies", some

00:02:52.251 --> 00:02:56.690
of the mud stains seem to have miraculously
disappeared.

00:02:56.690 --> 00:03:01.090
Maurice and Belle's horse, Philippe, is also
at the centre of several mistakes in the movie.

00:03:01.090 --> 00:03:05.200
The first one occurs when Maurice is attacked
by the wolves and Philippe bolts with his

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:07.110
harness and chains still attached.

00:03:07.110 --> 00:03:11.420
But, when Philippe returns to save Maurice
just before the wolves get him, he no longer

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:12.420
has them.

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:17.420
Next, after Maurice is captured by Beast at
the enchanted castle, Philippe gets away and

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:20.950
runs back home to Belle, arriving dirty and
muddy.

00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:24.830
Belle understands something has happened and
tells Philippe to take her to her father,

00:03:24.830 --> 00:03:27.750
except that when we see Belle riding, Philippe
is clean again.

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:31.710
Of course, it seems very unlikely Belle would
have stopped to clean Philippe as she was

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:33.990
rushing to look for her missing father.

00:03:33.990 --> 00:03:38.800
Later, when Maurice leaves the castle, we
don't see how he gets back to the town.

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:42.600
Philippe is still at the castle when Belle
flees and gets attacked by the wolves, so

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:44.830
Maurice didn't take Philippe with him.

00:03:44.830 --> 00:03:49.130
In the original animation, Maurice was sent
back on an enchanted carriage, but in the

00:03:49.130 --> 00:03:53.190
live-action remake, his return to town remains
a mystery.

00:03:53.190 --> 00:03:57.360
When Belle arrives at the castle she runs
up a staircase in a clockwise direction.

00:03:57.360 --> 00:04:02.330
Notice how she's holding the candlestick in
her right hand, which is closest to the inside

00:04:02.330 --> 00:04:04.010
wall of the stairs.

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:08.500
As she emerges at the top of the staircase,
her right hand and candlestick are closest

00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:13.290
to the outside wall and she's now running
anti-clockwise.

00:04:13.290 --> 00:04:18.409
Back in town, Gaston gets to perform his big
number, but just as LeFou starts singing Gaston's

00:04:18.409 --> 00:04:20.910
knife handling reveals a continuity error.

00:04:20.910 --> 00:04:25.840
Watch carefully how his right hand moves from
the hilt of the knife in this shot to all

00:04:25.840 --> 00:04:31.139
way down the blade near the tip when LeFou
is singing and the shot changes angle.

00:04:31.139 --> 00:04:35.529
Also during the song, Gaston shoots into the
ceiling, and a small pile of debris falls

00:04:35.529 --> 00:04:36.529
down.

00:04:36.529 --> 00:04:41.490
The song then continues, but from this camera
angle, the debris is no longer there.

00:04:41.490 --> 00:04:45.289
The live-action version of "Be Our Guest"
is just fantastic yet there are still a couple

00:04:45.289 --> 00:04:46.819
of mistakes in there.

00:04:46.819 --> 00:04:51.129
The guillotine-based joke that Lumiere makes
when he chops a baguette is anachronistic

00:04:51.129 --> 00:04:55.699
as the guillotine wasn't common in France
until the late 18th century, whereas the movie

00:04:55.699 --> 00:04:58.319
is actually set in the mid-18th century.

00:04:58.319 --> 00:05:02.379
Although the blade in the film is a bread
guillotine, Lumiere says "This Is France"

00:05:02.379 --> 00:05:06.199
as he chops the bread, and the guillotine
is, of course, closely associated with the

00:05:06.199 --> 00:05:07.809
French Revolution.

00:05:07.809 --> 00:05:12.660
Also the chopped baguette piece falls into
a little basket similar to how heads did after

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:13.669
executions.

00:05:13.669 --> 00:05:17.760
And on the menu, there's another French slip-up
with the Potato dishes, with a spelling mistake

00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:19.050
on "Pommes De Terre".

00:05:19.050 --> 00:05:23.360
The "terre" is spelled incorrectly with an
"s" on the end.

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:27.310
And when Lumiere introduces the dishes, he
mentions various plates that are supposed

00:05:27.310 --> 00:05:33.020
to appear on Belle's menu including Beef Ragout,
Cheese Soufflé, Pie and Pudding en Flambé,

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:39.120
except that Cheese Soufflé isn't on the menu,
it's Camembert Grillé.

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:42.919
When Belle and Beast go for a walk in the
castle grounds, she recites a line from a

00:05:42.919 --> 00:05:48.479
poem called A Crystal Forest, which goes as
follows: 'each blade of grass seems clad miraculously

00:05:48.479 --> 00:05:50.020
with glass'.

00:05:50.020 --> 00:05:55.090
That poem was penned by a Scottish writer
called William Sharp, who was born in 1855

00:05:55.090 --> 00:05:56.430
and died in 1905.

00:05:56.430 --> 00:06:01.493
However, as this movie is set in the mid-1700s,
there's no way Belle could have known a poem

00:06:01.493 --> 00:06:03.900
which hadn't been written yet!

00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:08.089
The owl we see with Agathe as she's nursing
Maurice gives a little hoot.

00:06:08.089 --> 00:06:13.469
However, the type of owl is actually a barn
owl and barn owls make screechy type of noises

00:06:13.469 --> 00:06:17.770
rather than the typical hoots you might expect
from other types of owl.

00:06:17.770 --> 00:06:22.870
After Belle and Maurice break out of the asylum
wagon, Belle rides off to the castle dumping

00:06:22.870 --> 00:06:24.850
her yellow dress as she leaves.

00:06:24.850 --> 00:06:28.800
She's obviously in a hurry as she knows Beast
is in danger, but during the ride back to

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:33.729
the castle she acquires a sweater, which doesn't
quite make sense because she got rid of it

00:06:33.729 --> 00:06:38.099
later anyway and surely she wouldn't have
taken the time to go home and pick up something

00:06:38.099 --> 00:06:39.099
new to wear?

00:06:39.099 --> 00:06:43.889
So, what other movie mistakes, goof or plot
holes did you spot in Beauty And The Beast?

